.TH CHANGELOG-COLLECTION-NEW 8 "July 2026" "changelog 1.0.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
changelog collection\-new \- initialize changelog directory for Ansible collections
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B changelog collection-new
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBcollection\-new\fR command initializes a new Ansible collection's changelog directory structure with appropriate defaults and configuration. It sets up the standard layout expected for Ansible collections, including plugin documentation generation capabilities.

This command is specifically designed for Ansible collection projects that need to track changes across multiple plugins and modules within the collection namespace.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.

.TP
\fB\-\-ansible\-doc\-bin\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Path to ansible-doc binary for plugin documentation generation. Overrides autodetection of the ansible-doc command in system PATH.

.TP
\fB\-\-use\-ansible\-doc\fR
Always use ansible-doc tool to find and document plugins, even if plugins directory exists. Forces regeneration of plugin metadata from source files.

.TP
\fB\-\-collection\-namespace\fR=\fINAMESPACE\fR
Override the collection namespace (e.g., "myorg.myplugin"). Used for generating fully qualified plugin names in documentation.

.TP
\fB\-\-collection\-name\fR=\fINAME\fR
Override the collection name portion of the namespace. Combined with \fB\-\-collection\-namespace\fR for complete identification.

.TP
\fB\-\-reload\-plugins\fR
Force reload of plugin cache during initialization. Useful when plugins have been added/removed since last generation.

.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\fR
Update existing entries from fragments and refresh plugin descriptions during initialization.

.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\-plugins\fR=\fIMODE\fR
Specify how to handle plugin description updates: "allow-removal" or "prevent-removal".

.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\-fragments\fR=\fIMODE\fR
Control which fragments to include during refresh: "without-archives" (default) or "with-archives".

.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-dir\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Changelog base directory. Defaults to current directory's \fIchangelogs/\fR subdirectory.
.SH DIRECTORY STRUCTURE CREATED
.PP
The command creates the standard Ansible collection changelog layout:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fIchangelogs/config.yaml\fR \- Collection-specific configuration with plugin documentation settings
.IP \(bu 2
\fIchangelogs/fragments/\fR \- Directory for fragment files describing individual changes
.IP \(bu 2
\fIplugins/\fR \- Plugin source directory (if not already present)
.RE

.TP
.B Configuration Defaults:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBis_collection: true\fR \- Marks this as a collection project
.IP \(bu 2
\fBusFQCN: true\fR \- Use fully qualified collection names in output
.IP \(bu 2
\fBadd_plugin_period: true\fR \- Add period after plugin names in documentation
.RE
.SH PLUGIN DOCUMENTATION
.PP
When \fB\-\-use\-ansible\-doc\fR is specified, the command integrates with ansible-doc to:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Scan plugins directory for all available plugins and modules
.IP \(bu 2
Extract documentation strings and parameter descriptions
.IP \(bu 2
Generate plugin reference sections in changelog output
.IP \(bu 2
Maintain metadata about plugin availability and changes
.RE

.TP
.B Use Cases:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Initializing a new Ansible collection with changelog support
.IP \(bu 2
Adding plugin documentation to existing collections
.IP \(bu 2
Regenerating plugin metadata after structural changes
.IP \(bu 2
Setting up CI/CD pipelines for collection releases
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Initialize a new collection:
.nf
    changelog collection-new --collection-namespace myorg.myplugin -d collections/my_collection
.fi

.TP
Initialize with plugin documentation generation:
.nf
    changelog collection-new \\
        --use-ansible-doc \\
        --collection-namespace community.general \\
        --reload-plugins
.fi

.TP
Refresh existing collection changelog:
.nf
    changelog collection-new \\
        --refresh \\
        --refresh-plugins allow-removal \\
        -d /path/to/existing/collection
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.TP
\fBchangelog-init(8)\fR \- Initialize general project changelog structure
.TP
\fBchangelog-release(8)\fR \- Generate release notes including plugin documentation
